<Base title="A little clarity for your next money move." description="About Howloop: free financial calculators and plain-English money education for people in Australia."><header class="hl-page-head hl-wrap"><div class="hl-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / about</div><span class="hl-eyebrow">HOWLOOP · THE DETAILS</span><h1 style="max-width:900px">A little clarity for your next money move.</h1></header><article class="hl-wrap hl-content"><p class="hl-page-meta">Updated 18 September 2026</p><h2>Why Howloop exists</h2><p>Money decisions often begin with a simple question: what could I save, what would the repayments be, or how much breathing room do I need? Howloop turns those questions into practical calculators and explanations for life in Australia.</p><p>Our focus is understandable numbers. The calculators separate your contributions from interest, show the assumptions behind a result and let you explore what changes when you adjust a plan.</p><h2>What you will find here</h2><ul><li>Free calculators for savings, home loans, goals and cash buffers.</li><li>A directory of public Australian banking product data, with retrieval dates and coverage limits.</li><li>Original explanations with worked examples and links to official sources.</li></ul><h2>Our role</h2><p>Howloop is an educational website, not a bank, lender, broker or personal financial advice service. We do not connect to your bank account, arrange financial products or assess what is suitable for your circumstances. Bank names identify products; they do not imply sponsorship or endorsement.</p><h2>How we keep things accountable</h2><p>You can inspect the <a href="/methodology">calculation methods</a>, follow each guide’s sources and <a href="/contact">report a correction</a>. We do not present automated calculations as professional review. Financial content is published under the Howloop name, and our <a href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a> explains how it is prepared.</p><h2>How the site is supported</h2><p>Howloop is free to use. We are preparing the site for advertising, which may help support its operation. The bank directory is alphabetical and does not sell ranking positions. Any future sponsorship or affiliate relationship should be disclosed where it appears.</p><h2>A note on our older guides</h2><p>Howloop began with everyday how-to guides. Those existing pages remain available in the <a href="/guides">guide archive</a>; the main site now focuses on Australian money tools.</p></article></Base>
